A Test of Words

In digital realms, a file is born,
A canvas blank, awaiting to adorn.
With letters typed and thoughts unfurled,
A poem emerges, a tiny world.

"testt.xt," an odd name it bears,
But within its bytes, a story shares.
Of creativity's spark and tech's embrace,
Where human and machine find common space.

So here it rests, this simple rhyme,
A test of storage, a mark of time.
In ones and zeros, yet full of heart,
Where poetry and data both take part.